        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The first step in analyzing a dense style is to look at subjects. If you do not see main characters as simple subjects, you have to look for them. They can be in objects of prepositions, in possessive pronouns, or in adjectives. Once you find them, look for actions they are involved in. When you are revising, make those characters the subjects of verbs expressing those actions. When you are reading a dense passage, try to find characters and their actions, and retell the story to yourself.",
            "block_bbox": [
                127,
                716,
                783,
                858
            ],
            "block_id": 17,
